  "reason": "The Lean statement uses `U.annihilator = ⊥` whereas the English statement refers to the orthogonal complement `U^{\\perp}`; these are different notions in mathlib, so the formalization does not match the intended claim."
}

{
  "verdict": "faithful",
  "reason": "The Lean statement asserts that there is no multiplicative equivalence (group isomorphism) between ℝˣ and ℂˣ, which exactly matches the English claim that the multiplicative groups ℝ\\{0} and ℂ\\{0} are not isomorphic."
}

{
  "verdict": "faithful",
  "reason": "The Lean statement includes exactly the same group, integer n > 1, the hypothesis (ab)^n = a^n b^n for all a,b, and concludes (aba^{-1}b^{-1})^{n*(n-1)} = 1 for all a,b, matching the English formulation."
}
